---
description: HTTP query/fetch functions live in lib/services, not lib/query.
globs: lib/query/**/*.{ts,tsx},lib/services/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Query functions live in `lib/services`

HTTP fetchers and React Query `queryFn` implementations belong in `lib/services/<name>/`. `lib/query` holds query keys, cache merge/ingest, persist, and hooks that *call* those fetchers.

Each service is a folder:

- `index.ts` — the implementation
- `types.ts` — params, function type, and return type

Re-export those types from `index.ts`. Do not add a `lib/services` barrel. Import the service folder.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — network I/O next to cache keys
// lib/query/sprint-board.ts
export const fetchSprintBoardFromHttp = async (sprintNumber?: number) => {
  const response = await fetch("/api/sprint-board");
  return response.json();
};

// ❌ BAD — nested folder named after the function
// lib/services/sprintBoard/fetchSprintBoardFromHttp/index.ts

// ✅ GOOD — service folder; types in types.ts, re-exported from index.ts
// lib/services/sprintBoard/types.ts
export type FetchSprintBoardParams = { sprintNumber?: number };
export type SprintBoardData = { /* return type */ };
export type FetchSprintBoard = (
  sprintNumber?: FetchSprintBoardParams["sprintNumber"],
) => Promise<SprintBoardData>;

// lib/services/sprintBoard/index.ts
export type { FetchSprintBoard, FetchSprintBoardParams, SprintBoardData } from "./types";
export const fetchSprintBoardFromHttp: FetchSprintBoard = async (sprintNumber) => { /* HTTP */ };

// lib/query/useSprintBoard.ts
import { fetchSprintBoardFromHttp } from "@/lib/services/sprintBoard";
import type { SprintBoardData } from "@/lib/services/sprintBoard";
```
